## Implementation Notes

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Volatility Focus**: Since straddle/strangle profitability depends heavily on volatility regime, we're implementing multiple volatility estimators (realized, Parkinson, Garman-Klass) and second-order Greeks (Vanna, Volga) that measure sensitivity to volatility changes.

> [!NOTE]
> **Feature Count**: Expanding from 5 to 55 features. This is justified because:
> - Volatility regime detection requires multiple estimators
> - Options trading needs comprehensive Greeks
> - Real-time adaptation requires multi-timeframe analysis

> [!CAUTION]
> **Black-Scholes for Everything**: Replacing the simplified option pricing model with full Black-Scholes implementation for both option pricing AND Greeks calculation. This ensures accuracy.

> [!TIP]
> **Performance**: Feature calculation will use vectorized operations and caching to maintain fast step times even with 60 features.
